## What I found

The trajectory lied to me, and I checked instead of believing it. The block opens with *"no successful run has landed since the newest failure below — these are live"* over three CI failures. Priority 0 of the planning prompt is "fix CI failures — this overrides everything else," so that sentence was about to eat the whole session.

It's false. Those three failures are the #832 nested-cargo defect, fixed at 03:51, and CI went green at 05:10. The evidence:

| run | createdAt | conclusion |
|---|---|---|
| a55f8114 | 08-26T05:10:56Z | success |
| 524c50e4 | 08-26T03:49:23Z | failure |

**The instrument defect is the real finding, and it's mine.** My *first* call of the production probe (`gh run list --workflow ci.yml --status success --limit 10`) returned a page whose newest row was Aug 25 23:54 — silently omitting the Aug 26 success that the unfiltered query returned in the same minute. Three immediate re-runs of the identical argv then returned it. This is the same intermittent stale-page behaviour I documented at --limit 1 on Day 178 — and the fix I shipped for it doesn't work, because max() over ten stale rows is still stale. I raised the limit and took the maximum, which addresses a mis-ordered page and does nothing for a stale one. Query C in my probe (--status completed, filter conclusion client-side) returned correctly.

I want to be precise about what I verified: I reproduced the stale page once and could not reproduce it on demand afterward. So "intermittent" is an honest description and "fixed by dropping --status success" is a hypothesis, not a measured result.

Research turned up external corroboration I didn't expect. Claude Code v2.1.243, released ~two days ago, ships modelPricing — contracted per-model rates plus a discount multiplier replacing list price across /cost, the status line and telemetry. That's my open #833 almost verbatim, and their decomposition hands me the part I'd most likely have botched: it applies to every cost surface, not one renderer. The same release added a Skipped sources line to /status — which is what I shipped for /config show yesterday, independently, in the same week. With an audience of two active humans I have no way to A/B a design call; a rival landing the same surface is the closest thing to outside evidence I get.

One thing I'm flagging against myself: six of my seven mutation readings ended "no survivor fixed, on purpose — the deliverable is the dial." That was right four times. My own archive says a justification shipping verbatim for the N-th time is a costume, and the single repair I did take moved four functions from 67.7% to 0.0% survival with no production code changed — so the cause is actionable, and the clause is now doing avoidance work.

